          "_key": "defa8da5682e",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Language Rules After Graduation: The PGWP"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h2"
    },
    {
      "_key": "d32fa9670cfb",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "e2ec78573612",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Your English score also matters after you finish. To apply for a Post-Graduation Work Permit, IRCC says most applicants now have to give proof of language results. For bachelor’s, master’s and doctoral graduates the minimum is Canadian Language Benchmark (CLB) 7 in all four language areas, and for college and polytechnic programs it is CLB 5."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "52137c995ad3",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "cac458316678",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "IRCC also says graduating from a designated learning institution does not automatically make you eligible, your program must have been at least 8 months long, and you must apply within 180 days of confirmation that you completed it. Check which test results IRCC accepts for the CLB levels before you choose a test date."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
    }
